coder › Implemented `debounce` in `src/debounce.ts` and added tests in `src/debounce.test.ts`.

What changed:
- `debounce` now throws `RangeError` when `ms < 0`.
- Returned function stores the most recent arguments, cancels any pending timer, and schedules a new one on every call.
- `cancel()` clears a pending timer and its arguments.
- `flush()` clears the pending timer and invokes `fn` immediately with the latest arguments; it is a no-op when nothing is pending.
- Timers are taken from the optional `timers` argument, defaulting to the global `setTimeout`/`clearTimeout`.
- Added fake-timer tests covering: delayed single call with latest args, timer reset on repeated calls, `cancel`, `flush`, no-op `cancel`/`flush`, the `RangeError`, and re-entry from inside the running function.

